    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, if the logs show the package was fine during transit, aren't we basically just paying for their mistake? If I tell the customer we're sending a replacement despite the logs showing no transit damage, aren't we incentivizing people to lie about broken items? I don't want to get a reputation for being a pushover if the data says they're wrong.",
